{"label":"2A","direction":"against","claim":"Fred Hutch's core raised NovaSeq X Plus lane prices about 3% on both tiers between a search-snippet capture and its 3 Sep 2026 page edit, so this core shows no discounting.","detail":"I fetched the live page. The 10B lane is now $1,494 internal/consortium and $2,629.44 external. The earlier snippet showed $1,450 and $2,552. That is +3.03% internal (1494/1450) and +3.03% external (2629.44/2552), a uniform pass-through. The page gives no effective date, only 'Last Modified, September 03, 2026'. I could not date the snippet version because Wayback is blocked from my tool. The 25B lane is $2,472 internal and $4,351 external. The page mentions no discounts.","url":"https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/shared-resources/core-facilities/genomics-bioinformatics/rates-scheduling.html","date":"2026-09-03","source_name":"Fred Hutch Genomics core rate page","source_type":"price_list","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Fred Hutch is a new core. The 3.0% increase is the first dated change quantified there, and the known list shows only a ~3% increase at TxGen."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"At Fred Hutch the 10B lane costs about 1.5x the 25B lane per Gb. Within-X price steps are steep, so a 35B flow cell priced on the same curve would pull the 25B price down.","detail":"A 25B lane is 3.1–4B read pairs. At PE151 (302 bases per pair) that is about 936–1,208 Gb. At $2,472 internal that is about $2.05–2.64/Gb. A 10B lane is 1.25–1.5B pairs, about 377–453 Gb. At $1,494 that is about $3.30–3.96/Gb. The ratio is about 1.5x internal. External: 25B $4,351 is about $3.60–4.65/Gb and 10B $2,629 is about $5.80–6.97/Gb, also about 1.5x. Output is nominal and not measured. These are cores, not Illumina's net prices.","url":"https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/shared-resources/core-facilities/genomics-bioinformatics/rates-scheduling.html","date":"2026-09-03","source_name":"Fred Hutch Genomics core rate page","source_type":"price_list","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"A new core's 10B/25B ladder. Known ladders include Pitt 1.5x and KUMC 1.03x, but not Fred Hutch."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"Outside users at Fred Hutch pay 76% more than internal users on the 25B lane as well, and 76% on the 10B lane. Research pricing is heavily tiered, so a large external buyer has room to negotiate down.","detail":"The 25B lane is $4,351 external vs $2,472 internal, which is 1.76x (+76%). The 10B lane is $2,629.44 vs $1,494, also 1.76x. Both lanes use one uniform external multiplier. It looks like a core recharge policy, not an Illumina discount. The NextSeq 2000 tiers are 1.76x (P1-100: 2,988/1,697) and 1.76x (P4-300: 5,674/3,224).","url":"https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/shared-resources/core-facilities/genomics-bioinformatics/rates-scheduling.html","date":"2026-09-03","source_name":"Fred Hutch Genomics core rate page","source_type":"price_list","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This adds the 25B-lane premium and shows the premium is uniform across flow cells. The known list has the 76% figure only on the 10B snippet."},
