{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"At Oregon the 6000 S4 costs about 6.8–8.5 dollars per Gb, which is 2.6–4x Fred Hutch's 25B internal per-Gb price. A 6000 lab that converts would get a deep cut.","detail":"S4-300 is $5,070 internal for 2–2.5B read pairs. At 300 bases per pair that is 600–750 Gb, or $6.76–8.45/Gb. Fred Hutch's 25B is $2.05–2.64/Gb internal. The cross-core ratio is about 2.6x (6.76/2.64) up to 4.1x (8.45/2.05). The overlap is wide because the two cores state nominal ranges, not measured output. Smaller flow cells are higher: SP-300 is $2,318 for 325–400M pairs, or $5.8–7.1/Gb.","url":"https://gc3f.uoregon.edu/rates","date":"2026","source_name":"University of Oregon GC3F rates page; Fred Hutch rate page","source_type":"price_list","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This pairs a new X core with Oregon's S4. The known list has the Oregon-to-Berkeley ratio only."},
